          "objectId": "project-0",
          "title": "MIT CBA",
          "description": "MIT’s Center for Bits and Atoms used the xTool MetalFab to design and mill custom replacement parts for an aging bicycle—combining rapid prototyping with precision metal fabrication. This project shows how simple digital fabrication can revive everyday objects and help students tackle real engineering challenges.",
          "image": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0467/7985/9095/files/mk-1_25forthemakers_us_pc_frame1329132190_1066-6244_c33f3f7e-29df-4e74-97e8-49fa3b7add59.webp?v=1764752216",
          "link": {
            "label": "Read the Case Study",
            "href": "https://eperry.notion.site/Custom-Parts-for-an-Old-Bike-using-the-xTool-MetalFab-23dd2e30b48c800dad9df4b1f0fcb1c5"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
